#. engine/messages/decoders_agree.py (ticket 10): the decoder cross-check's codes.
msgid "engine.decoders_agree.disagree"
msgstr "The two readers found different contents in this file: {items, plural, =0 {they found the same items but disagree on what some of them are} one {# item was found by only one of them} other {# items were found by only one of them}}{layers, plural, =0 {} one {, on # layer} other {, on # layers}}{unread, plural, =0 {} one {; the second reader could not read # item} other {; the second reader could not read # items}}. It is held, so nothing from it reaches the sheet list while it may be misread."

msgid "engine.decoders_agree.not_installed"
msgstr "This file was read once, not twice: the second reader could not run, which is a fault on Vextrus's side, not in your file. Nothing from it reaches the sheet list; mark it for Vextrus to check."

msgid "engine.decoders_agree.not_pinned"
msgstr "This file was read once, not twice: the second reader could not run, which is a fault on Vextrus's side, not in your file. Nothing from it reaches the sheet list; mark it for Vextrus to check."

msgid "engine.decoders_agree.stopped"
msgstr "This file was read once, not twice: the second reader stopped before it finished, which is a fault on Vextrus's side, not in your file. Nothing from it reaches the sheet list; mark it for Vextrus to check."

msgid "engine.decoders_agree.too_many"
msgstr "This file was read once, not twice: it is larger than the second reader can check (up to {limit, plural, one {# item} other {# items}}). Nothing from it reaches the sheet list; mark it for Vextrus to check."
